<h1>Python Course</h1>

<p>A slide-deck-driven course covering Python, web development with Django and FastAPI, testing, tooling, and a few extras.</p>

<h2>Python language</h2>
<ul>
  <li><a href="introduction.html">Introduction</a><br><small>What we'll cover, why Python, course structure.</small></li>
  <li><a href="python-basics.html">Python basics</a><br><small>Types, control flow, functions, comprehensions, exceptions.</small></li>
  <li><a href="oop.html">Object-oriented programming</a><br><small>Classes, inheritance, dunders, dataclasses, ABCs, Protocols.</small></li>
  <li><a href="metaprogramming.html">Metaprogramming</a><br><small>Decorators, descriptors, metaclasses, <code>__init_subclass__</code>.</small></li>
  <li><a href="refactoring-python.html">Refactoring Python</a><br><small>Code smells, SOLID, idiomatic improvements.</small></li>
  <li><a href="patterns.html">Design patterns</a><br><small>Why half of them disappear in Python.</small></li>
</ul>

<h2>Tooling &amp; testing</h2>
<ul>
  <li><a href="python-tooling.html">Project setup with uv</a><br><small>Install Python, scaffold projects, manage deps and tools — <code>uv</code>, the modern default.</small></li>
  <li><a href="python-packages.html">Python packages — under the hood</a><br><small>What <code>uv</code> abstracts: <code>pip</code>, <code>venv</code>, <code>pyproject.toml</code>, publishing to PyPI.</small></li>
  <li><a href="task-runners.html">Task runners</a><br><small>Make, <code>invoke</code>, <code>click</code>, <code>typer</code> for project commands.</small></li>
  <li><a href="pytest.html">PyTest</a><br><small>Fixtures, parametrize, marks, mocking, plugins.</small></li>
  <li><a href="static-code-analysis.html">Static code analysis</a><br><small><code>ruff</code>, <code>mypy</code>, <code>pre-commit</code>.</small></li>
  <li><a href="continuous_integration.html">Continuous integration</a><br><small>Running tests, lint, and type-check on every push.</small></li>
</ul>

